+<!-- decision-log body. `wingfoil memory add` copies this scaffold verbatim; `memory submit` replaces
+     these placeholder comments with real content and fills the required frontmatter fields. -->
+
+# Decision — applyPatch rejects sparse patches and non-JSON values
+
+## Context
+An operation's `value` must be a JSON value (RFC 6902 section 4), and each element of a patch is an
+operation. `reduce` skipped holes in sparse arrays, and `structuredClone` accepted values JSON cannot hold.
+
+## Decision
+- Holes in the patch array are read as `undefined` and fail as invalid operations.
+- `value` must be null, boolean, string, finite number, array without holes, or plain object, recursively;
+  otherwise the patch is invalid.
+
+## Consequences
+Patches that could not have come from JSON text now fail instead of producing results that do not
+round-trip through JSON. Validation walks each value once more.
